{"name":"Dreamy Memory","hex":"#e8c3d9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dreamy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["As in a dream; resembling a dream.","Sexy; handsome; attractive."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dreamy"},{"term":"memory","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The ability of the brain to record information or impressions with the facility of recalling them later, usually at will.","A record of a thing or an event stored and available for later use by an organism."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/memory"}],"entries":[{"title":"Memory","blocks":[{"text":"Memory is the faculty of the mind by which data or information is encoded, stored, and retrieved when needed. It is the retention of information over time for the purpose of influencing future action. If past events could not be remembered, it would be impossible for language, relationships, or personal identity to develop. Memory loss is usually described as forgetfulness or a disorder such as amnesia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Memory.gif/330px-Memory.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Memory","wikidata":"Q492"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Memory-Warner-Highsmith.jpeg/500px-Memory-Warner-Highsmith.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Memory-Warner-Highsmith.jpeg/1280px-Memory-Warner-Highsmith.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Memory-Warner-Highsmith.jpeg/500px-Memory-Warner-Highsmith.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Olin Levi Warner's 1896 illustration, Memory, now housed in the Thomas Jefferson Bui